  "mean_bias_mechanisms": [
   "Linear response: white zero-mean force noise adds variance only; <F> unchanged. CQ models reproduce the Newtonian mean (Tilloy-Diosi 2017 Eq. 10: unitary pair potential + double commutator; Kryhin-Sudhir Eq. 5: averaged Poisson equation sourced by <f>).",
   "DP/CQ self-noise is independent of source-mass position (Stage 29), so any heating-induced shift is identical in both source configurations and cancels in the near-far difference that defines G.",
   "Second-order (rectification) via amplitude-dependent torsion period: bounded above (column rectification_bias_ppm) with generous inputs.",
   "Matter-sourced (discrete) kernel: noise near the source mass differs between configurations, but enters as variance; bounded above (matter_sourced_ppm)."
  ]
 },
